cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these benchmarks, please cite them as below."
title: "Computer algebra system benchmarks: reproducible, verified and dated benchmarks of CAS reachable from Julia"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Celles
    given-names: Sébastien
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9987-4338"
    affiliation: "IUT de Poitiers, Université de Poitiers"
repository-code: "https://github.com/s-celles/computer_algebra_system_benchmarks"
url: "https://s-celles.github.io/computer_algebra_system_benchmarks/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - computer algebra
  - symbolic computation
  - Julia
  - Giac
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  Five benches of computer algebra systems reachable from Julia (Giac.jl,
  Symbolics.jl, SymPy through SymPyPythonCall.jl, SymJ.jl, Primes.jl and
  LibPARI.jl): FFI overhead, CAS operations, integer factorisation,
  functional coverage and a 107-problem suite. Fixed inputs, one adapter per
  system, every answer checked by a system-neutral test, every run dated and
  its environment pinned. The reproduced numbers of the JuliaCon Proceedings
  paper on Giac.jl.
